Revision history for SICK-Target-Proxmox

{{$NEXT}}
    - Initial release
    - Device types proxmox-ve (SICK::Target::ProxmoxVE) and proxmox-bs
      (SICK::Target::ProxmoxBS): certificate, chain and key are uploaded
      through the node's own API (POST /api2/json/nodes/<node>/certificates/
      custom); the API token is read from a file and sent only in the
      request header.
    - The connection to the node is always verified, against the ca files
      and/or SHA-256 fingerprint pins of the device list only: no system
      store, no proxy, no redirects, nothing in the environment can loosen
      it. A node that fails the check gets no request.
    - Key, certificate and leaf-first chain are checked before anything is
      sent; the answer must name the uploaded certificate; error messages
      never quote the token, the key or the body.
    - Tests run against a Perl stand-in of both APIs, including checks that
      the token does not leak.
    - Both device types ran end to end through `sick run` against a real
      PVE 9.2.21 API (pveproxy restarted through a systemctl shim, no
      systemd, no cluster) and a real PBS 4.2.8-1, each in a container with
      the lab CA (t/e2e/device-proxmox.sh). Not tried: under systemd, in a
      cluster, across a real network.
